   "choices": [
    "Gone — delete the checkbox and the glossary entry too",
    "Switched off — put the source back on the flow, leave it unchecked",
    "Gone as it stands, but the capability comes back differently"
   ],
   "detail": "Those are two different acts and you did both in one breath. Unchecking the box means 'not in the next run' — an operational toggle, and the source still exists. Deleting the node from the run flow means the source is not part of Argus any more. Only one of them should survive, and the drawings currently assert both.\n\nIt matters for what I do next. If it is gone, the checkbox goes, the glossary entry goes, the DataSource tooltip on the domain model drops to four, and the fifth source that took months to bolt on gets removed in an afternoon. If it is switched off, the source belongs back on the flow with the box unchecked, and 'noisy' becomes a tuning problem rather than a decommissioning.\n\nThe third option is the one I would push for. Macro data is not obviously worthless — it is unfiltered. Routing it through enrichment as a scored signal would put it behind the same confidence gate as everything else, at which point 'noisy' has a dial instead of a switch.",
   "examples": [
    "Gone: nobody has looked at a Fed date in the output in months",
    "Off for now: it is noisy in this market, not always",
    "Rebuild it as a scored signal so the 0.70 gate applies to it"
   ],
   "id": "tw-16-1",
   "question": "You deleted Macro Calendar from the run flow and unchecked it on the console. Is it gone from the product, or switched off for now?"
